WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.010
"Danger for all Reds?" Gliss cried, echoing the crow's warning. "What does that mean?"

2
00:00:06.011 --> 00:00:10.935
"Hush," Professor Liblow said again. "Let it finish its message."

3
00:00:10.936 --> 00:00:13.412
Echo crows didn't talk on their own.

4
00:00:13.413 --> 00:00:16.290
They could only repeat what a person told them.

5
00:00:16.291 --> 00:00:20.356
The crow flapped its wings. "Urgent danger," it said again.

6
00:00:20.357 --> 00:00:26.003
"Reds are disappearing all over Magica. Nobody knows where they went or what has become of them.

7
00:00:26.004 --> 00:00:30.496
All Reds, please take precautions. Urgent, urgent."

8
00:00:30.497 --> 00:00:34.888
The echo crow clacked its beak. Then it flew out of the room.

9
00:00:34.889 --> 00:00:40.142
Everyone started talking at once. Well, almost everyone.

10
00:00:40.143 --> 00:00:44.709
Zann didn't say a word. The crow's message had made him think about his parents.

11
00:00:44.710 --> 00:00:48.245
Nobody knew where they were either, or what had become of them.

12
00:00:48.246 --> 00:00:51.633
But that was different. For one thing, they weren't Reds.

13
00:00:51.634 --> 00:00:55.818
For another, they had disappeared four long years ago.

14
00:00:55.819 --> 00:01:01.754
Perda poked him. "Did you hear that?" she said. "What do you think it means?"

15
00:01:01.755 --> 00:01:09.546
"Silence!" Professor Liblow cried. His voice boomed, with the help of a Swelling spell.

16
00:01:09.547 --> 00:01:13.504
The class quieted down at once. Gliss raised her hand.

17
00:01:13.505 --> 00:01:16.822
"I need to go home," she said, her voice cracking.

18
00:01:16.823 --> 00:01:22.116
"Both of my parents are Reds. I should tell them about this warning!"

19
00:01:22.117 --> 00:01:26.956
"Me too," Zann said. "My grandfather, Boz, is a Red."

20
00:01:26.957 --> 00:01:32.179
"What's the big deal?" Jev's voice was loud enough for Zann to hear, but not the teacher.

21
00:01:32.180 --> 00:01:36.459
"All those snooty Reds are probably sneaking off somewhere together.

22
00:01:36.460 --> 00:01:41.480
Maybe they're trying to come up with even more ways to act superior to the rest of us."

23
00:01:41.481 --> 00:01:46.849
"Be quiet, Jev." Perda glared at him. "You're just jealous."

24
00:01:46.850 --> 00:01:52.789
Gliss hadn't heard Jev. She stood up. "I just remembered something," she said.

25
00:01:52.790 --> 00:01:56.180
"Last night I overheard my parents whispering."

26
00:01:56.181 --> 00:02:02.691
"You overheard them?" Professor Liblow gave her a suspicious look. "How?"

27
00:02:02.692 --> 00:02:07.132
Gliss blushed. "Okay, I admit it. I used a spy fly.

28
00:02:07.133 --> 00:02:10.282
I know we're not supposed to use them to spy on people.

29
00:02:10.283 --> 00:02:13.937
But my parents wouldn't tell me why they look so worried lately.

30
00:02:13.938 --> 00:02:16.994
I had to find out what's going on!"

31
00:02:16.995 --> 00:02:23.140
"Wow," thought Zann. If Gliss had used a spy fly, she must have been very concerned.

32
00:02:23.141 --> 00:02:26.066
"So what did you hear?" he asked.

33
00:02:26.067 --> 00:02:30.463
"It was about my uncle," Gliss said. "He lives in New Mist."

34
00:02:30.464 --> 00:02:33.821
"You mean the town near Mount Mystery?" Zann said.

35
00:02:33.822 --> 00:02:40.556
"My parents haven't heard from Uncle Gar in three days," Gliss said. "He's a Red too."

36
00:02:40.557 --> 00:02:46.615
"Oh dear." Professor Liblow shook his head. "This sounds rather serious.

37
00:02:46.616 --> 00:02:52.151
Perhaps you'd better go home . . . It's almost time to go anyway. Class dismissed."

38
00:02:52.152 --> 00:02:56.410
The students started gathering their things and chattering about what had just happened.

39
00:02:56.411 --> 00:03:01.952
Zann grabbed his bag and hurried out of the room with Perda.

40
00:03:01.953 --> 00:03:05.783
"I should find out what Boz knows about this," Zann said.

41
00:03:05.784 --> 00:03:12.732
"He's a retired Magic Master, remember? Maybe some of his friends in the capital know what's going

42
00:03:12.733 --> 00:03:17.273
on." Perda gave him a look. "You sound almost excited," she

43
00:03:17.274 --> 00:03:20.600
said. "Aren't you scared? You and Boz are both

44
00:03:20.601 --> 00:03:25.111
Reds." Before Zann could respond, Jev came into the hall with some

45
00:03:25.112 --> 00:03:29.478
friends. "Rushing home to hide under your bed, Red?" Jev

46
00:03:29.479 --> 00:03:38.951
jeered. Zann didn't answer. Jev had never forgiven him for an incident on Zann's first day at the Swamp Bottom School almost four years

47
00:03:38.952 --> 00:03:45.244
earlier. But even if that had never happened, they still wouldn't be friends. Jev seemed to hate all

48
00:03:45.245 --> 00:03:54.338
Reds. Well, not all Reds. Just then Gliss hurried out of the classroom, and Jev's voice instantly changed from sneering to

49
00:03:54.339 --> 00:03:58.836
sympathetic. "Hey, Gliss. Sorry your uncle is missing. Want me to walk you

50
00:03:58.837 --> 00:04:02.664
home?" "Thanks, that's sweet. But I'm in too much of a hurry to

51
00:04:02.665 --> 00:04:08.555
walk." Gliss rubbed her hands together and muttered the word "zap." A second later she

52
00:04:08.556 --> 00:04:14.320
disappeared. Jev frowned and then zapped himself away too. Zann was glad to see him

53
00:04:14.321 --> 00:04:21.430
go. "Come on," he told Perda. "I'll walk you home in case you're afraid of disappearing without a

54
00:04:21.431 --> 00:04:24.966
trace." "I'm not the one who should be afraid," she

55
00:04:24.967 --> 00:04:27.908
retorted. "The crow said the warning was only for

56
00:04:27.909 --> 00:04:32.083
Reds." "Okay," Zann said. "Then you can walk me

57
00:04:32.084 --> 00:04:35.267
home." She smiled. "It's a deal. Let's

58
00:04:35.268 --> 00:04:45.097
go." They headed for home. It was a bright, clear day with a light breeze that blew Perda's soft, caramel-colored hair around her

59
00:04:45.098 --> 00:04:48.940
face. Was it magic, or did she seem to get prettier every

60
00:04:48.941 --> 00:04:57.244
day? Zann tried not to notice that. It made him feel confused and nervous—a lot more nervous than he’d felt on hearing the echo crow's message.

61
00:04:57.245 --> 00:05:03.860
When they reached Perda's house, she sighed. "Looks like Mom's been redecorating again."

62
00:05:03.861 --> 00:05:11.030
The house had been square and blue that morning when the kids left for school. Now it was a multicolored blob.

63
00:05:11.031 --> 00:05:15.284
"Hey, she lives in Swamp Bottom, remember?" Zann joked.

64
00:05:15.285 --> 00:05:18.371
"She has to do something to lessen the boredom."

65
00:05:18.372 --> 00:05:22.441
Perda rolled her eyes. "See you tomorrow," she said.

66
00:05:22.442 --> 00:05:33.941
"Bye." Zann headed next door. His grandfather wasn't very interested in redecorating, so their house looked the same as always.

67
00:05:33.942 --> 00:05:38.169
In other words, it was just as boring as everything else in Swamp Bottom.

68
00:05:38.170 --> 00:05:42.094
For a second Zann wondered how his mother might redecorate the place.

69
00:05:42.095 --> 00:05:44.568
She'd always been good at that sort of thing.

70
00:05:44.569 --> 00:05:50.105
She'd loved to surprise him by turning his bedroom into a spooky cave or a mysterious jungle . . .

71
00:05:50.106 --> 00:05:54.241
He snapped out of those thoughts when he heard a rustling sound directly overhead.

72
00:05:54.242 --> 00:05:59.640
Glancing up, he barely had time to take in a dragon's snarling face hissing down at him.

73
00:05:59.641 --> 00:06:10.782
Zann jumped back just in time. A bolt of flame sizzled down, incinerating the ground where he'd just stood.

